{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120455","id":3899722424,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7ocQq4","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120455","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120455.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120455.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120455","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120455/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120455/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120455/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2cbad73358794a0e424fc127b2be8d1f15097080","number":120455,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix error spam by assuring `Bone2D` length","user":{"login":"Kapparoti","id":145791332,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLCZZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145791332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti","html_url":"https://github.com/Kapparoti","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kapparoti/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes [74266](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/74266)\r\n\r\nA Bone2D with a length <= 0 is not handled and spams errors while trying to render its polygon in the editor.\r\n\r\nThe length export range has a minimum of 1, but its not enforced in the setter function, so using a simple `set_length(0)` creates this situation:\r\n<img width=\"744\" height=\"392\" alt=\"ErrorSpam\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9fd064f2-e1ef-4cd0-b428-b613179326d3\" />\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe length minimum value done in the export range is also not documented.\r\n`p_list->push_back(PropertyInfo(Variant::FLOAT, PNAME(\"length\"), PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE, \"1, 1024, 1\", PROPERTY_USAGE_DEFAULT));`\r\n\r\nI limited the length to 1 like the export range does now, but (for its polygon rendering) it could also go without problems to a near-zero value of 1e-05 to avoid exactly 0. Should the export range be reduced to give that possibility?\r\n\r\nI also added a Warning to not change the user's value silently without them knowing.\r\n## Minimal reproduction project\r\nA clearer minimal reproduction than the one in the issue:\r\n[BoneLength.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29142299/BoneLength.zip)","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.git